  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506590</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Put people, especially women and youth, at the centre of the digital transformation through bringing CSOs&#x2019; voices from both the Global North and the Global South to the multilateral global system. It responds to both specific objectives by enhancing the capacities and capabilities of CSOs to engage more actively in the digital rights debate within multilateral- and multi-stakeholder- fora; byincreasing the cooperation between organisations based in the Global-North and in the Global-South to create safer online civic spaces and reduce the digital gap, especially addressing gender equality issues of digitalisation through prioritizing women&#x2019;s organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OXFAM IRELAND</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib registered in Tunisia in the end of 2011 and opened an office here early 2012.  Oxfam#s work in the Maghreb is a multi country program comprising Morocco, Tunisia, Algeria and Libya.  It supports local projects, is involved in lobby-work to take into account the interests of the poorest people, and campaigns to involve citizens in our work.  It#s focus in the Maghreb is on social and political participation, gender justice and supporting sustainable livelihoods work.  Four Oxfam affiliates work in the Maghreb:Oxfam Novib (The Netherlands), Intermon Oxfam (Spain), Oxfam Italy and Oxfam in Belgium. Oxfam has been working in the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) region for over five decades and over the past four decades promoting gender equality and supporting women#sright to participate and be represented in governance and decision-making structures and processes.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
  </participating-org>
